IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc14-part13-attempts.l4 -- PART XIII "Attempts -- Conspiracies -- Accessories" (ss 463 to 467) of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46.
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. Imports the keel's core (`ccc-core`).
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); it is not the official text.
-- SEAMS (PLAN.md section 6, row ccc14): ss 463 to 465 take what the offence attempted, counselled or conspired to be committed IS as inputs: its Class of offence and its Punishment
--   (the indictable limb, or the only limb), as the section that creates that offence answers them (every offence section of this folder answers `s N the class of the offence` and `s N the punishment`).
-- HOW A RESULT READS: JUST TRUE = the text brings the case within the provision; JUST FALSE = the text says no in its own words; NOTHING = not covered (see NOTES.md).
-- The punishments the sections give are answered as a LIST OF Punishment, one per limb (an indictable limb and, where the text makes the offence a hybrid, a summary limb).

§ `PART XIII -- Attempts -- Conspiracies -- Accessories`

§§ `Arithmetic on a term of imprisonment (the core's Length of time), used by ss 463 and 465`

-- A term as a count of whole months (years and months only; the days are kept apart).
GIVEN term IS A `Length of time`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 463 the months in the term` MEANS term's years TIMES 12 PLUS term's months

-- "fourteen years or less": a term of fourteen years or less. A term stated "less a day" is below its stated length.
GIVEN term IS A `Length of time`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 463 the term is fourteen years or less` MEANS
    `s 463 the months in the term` term LESS THAN 168
        OR (`s 463 the months in the term` term EQUALS 168 AND (term's days EQUALS 0 OR term's `less a day`))

-- "less than 14 years": the term is below fourteen years.
GIVEN term IS A `Length of time`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 463 the term is less than fourteen years` MEANS
    `s 463 the months in the term` term LESS THAN 168
        OR (`s 463 the months in the term` term EQUALS 168 AND term's days EQUALS 0 AND term's `less a day`)

-- "one-half of the longest term": the text does not say how to halve a term stated "less a day", or how to divide an odd number of months or days.
-- Years and months are halved together (so five years is two years and six months); an odd month or an odd number of days is not covered.
GIVEN term IS A `Length of time`
GIVETH A MAYBE (`Length of time`)
`s 463 one-half of the longest term` MEANS
    IF term's `less a day`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text does not say what one-half of a term stated "less a day" is
    ELSE IF `s 463 the months in the term` term MODULO 2 EQUALS 1 OR term's days MODULO 2 EQUALS 1
         THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text does not say how to halve an odd month or an odd day
         ELSE JUST (`Length of time` OF FLOOR ((`s 463 the months in the term` term DIVIDED BY 2) DIVIDED BY 12), (`s 463 the months in the term` term DIVIDED BY 2) MODULO 12, term's days DIVIDED BY 2, FALSE)

-- One limb of the punishments below: guilty of an indictable offence and liable to the stated imprisonment.
GIVEN imprisonment IS AN Imprisonment
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 463 punishment by indictment: imprisonment` MEANS
    Punishment OF `by indictment`, imprisonment, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

-- A limb that says only "guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction": the section states no term and no fine.
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 463 punishment on summary conviction: none stated in the section` MEANS
    Punishment OF `on summary conviction`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

§§ `s 463 -- Attempts, accessories`

-- src:8433 | 463 Except where otherwise expressly provided by law, the following provisions apply in respect of persons who attempt to commit or are accessories after the fact to the commission of offences:
-- src:8434 | (a) every one who attempts to commit or is an accessory after the fact to the commission of an indictable offence for which, on conviction, an accused is liable to be sentenced to imprisonment for life is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding fourteen years;
-- src:8435 | (b) every one who attempts to commit or is an accessory after the fact to the commission of an indictable offence for which, on conviction, an accused is liable to imprisonment for fourteen years or less is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term that is one-half of the longest term to which a person who is guilty of that offence is liable;
-- src:8436 | (c) every one who attempts to commit or is an accessory after the fact to the commission of an offence punishable on summary conviction is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction; and
-- src:8437 | (d) every one who attempts to commit or is an accessory after the fact to the commission of an offence for which the offender may be prosecuted by indictment or for which he is punishable on summary conviction
-- src:8438 | (i) is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding a term that is one-half of the longest term to which a person who is guilty of that offence is liable, or
-- src:8439 | (ii) is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 463 (src:8433-8439)
GIVEN `the person attempts to commit, or is an accessory after the fact to the commission of, an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the law expressly provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 463 the person is guilty of an offence by attempting, or by being an accessory after the fact` MEANS
    IF `the law expressly provides otherwise`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Except where otherwise expressly provided by law"
    ELSE IF `the person attempts to commit, or is an accessory after the fact to the commission of, an offence`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "persons who attempt to commit or are accessories after the fact to the commission of offences"

@ref s 463 (src:8433-8439)
GIVEN `the class of the offence attempted` IS A `Class of offence`
      `the punishment of the offence attempted, its indictable limb or its only limb` IS A Punishment
      `the law expressly provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF Punishment)
`s 463 the punishment for attempting to commit, or being an accessory after the fact to, an offence` MEANS
    IF `the law expressly provides otherwise`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Except where otherwise expressly provided by law"
    ELSE CONSIDER `the class of the offence attempted`
         WHEN `an offence punishable on summary conviction` THEN JUST (LIST `s 463 punishment on summary conviction: none stated in the section`)   -- (c)
         WHEN `an indictable offence` THEN
             CONSIDER `the punishment of the offence attempted, its indictable limb or its only limb`'s `maximum imprisonment`
             WHEN `no imprisonment is stated` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the offence section states no longest term, so neither (a) nor (b) can be applied
             WHEN `imprisonment for life` THEN JUST (LIST `s 463 punishment by indictment: imprisonment` (`imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`))   -- (a)
             WHEN `imprisonment for a term of` longest THEN
                 IF `s 463 the term is fourteen years or less` longest
                 THEN CONSIDER `s 463 one-half of the longest term` longest
                      WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): one-half of the longest term cannot be worked out from the text
                      WHEN JUST half THEN JUST (LIST `s 463 punishment by indictment: imprisonment` (`imprisonment for a term of` half))   -- (b)
                 ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a term above fourteen years that is not imprisonment for life is within neither (a) nor (b)
         WHEN `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction` THEN
             CONSIDER `the punishment of the offence attempted, its indictable limb or its only limb`'s `maximum imprisonment`
             WHEN `no imprisonment is stated` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the offence section states no longest term, so (d)(i) cannot be applied
             WHEN `imprisonment for life` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text does not say what one-half of imprisonment for life is
             WHEN `imprisonment for a term of` longest THEN
                 CONSIDER `s 463 one-half of the longest term` longest
                 WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): one-half of the longest term cannot be worked out from the text
                 WHEN JUST half THEN JUST (LIST `s 463 punishment by indictment: imprisonment` (`imprisonment for a term of` half), `s 463 punishment on summary conviction: none stated in the section`)   -- (d)(i) and (d)(ii)

-- The class of the offence of attempting depends on the class of the offence attempted: (a) and (b) make it an indictable offence, (c) an offence punishable on summary conviction, (d) both.
@ref s 463 (src:8433-8439)
GIVEN `the class of the offence attempted` IS A `Class of offence`
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 463 the class of the offence of attempting, or of being an accessory after the fact` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the class of the offence attempted`
    WHEN `an indictable offence` THEN `an indictable offence`   -- (a), (b)
    WHEN `an offence punishable on summary conviction` THEN `an offence punishable on summary conviction`   -- (c)
    WHEN `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction` THEN `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`   -- (d)

§§ `s 464 -- Counselling offence that is not committed`

-- src:8441 | 464 Except where otherwise expressly provided by law, the following provisions apply in respect of persons who counsel other persons to commit offences, namely,
-- src:8442 | (a) every one who counsels another person to commit an indictable offence is, if the offence is not committed, guilty of an indictable offence and liable to the same punishment to which a person who attempts to commit that offence is liable; and
-- src:8443 | (b) every one who counsels another person to commit an offence punishable on summary conviction is, if the offence is not committed, guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 464 (src:8441-8443)
GIVEN `the person counsels another person to commit an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence counselled is committed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the law expressly provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 464 the person is guilty of an offence by counselling an offence that is not committed` MEANS
    IF `the law expressly provides otherwise`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Except where otherwise expressly provided by law"
    ELSE IF NOT `the person counsels another person to commit an offence`
         THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "every one who counsels another person to commit an indictable offence"
         ELSE IF `the offence counselled is committed`
              THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the offence is not committed"
              ELSE JUST TRUE

@ref s 464 (src:8441-8443)
GIVEN `the class of the offence counselled` IS A `Class of offence`
      `the punishment of the offence counselled, its indictable limb or its only limb` IS A Punishment
      `the law expressly provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF Punishment)
`s 464 the punishment for counselling an offence that is not committed` MEANS
    IF `the law expressly provides otherwise`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Except where otherwise expressly provided by law"
    ELSE CONSIDER `the class of the offence counselled`
         WHEN `an indictable offence` THEN   -- (a): the same punishment as an attempt to commit that offence
             `s 463 the punishment for attempting to commit, or being an accessory after the fact to, an offence` `an indictable offence` `the punishment of the offence counselled, its indictable limb or its only limb` FALSE
         WHEN `an offence punishable on summary conviction` THEN JUST (LIST `s 463 punishment on summary conviction: none stated in the section`)   -- (b)
         WHEN `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): paragraphs (a) and (b) name an indictable offence and an offence punishable on summary conviction; the text of s 463(d) treats a hybrid as a third class

@ref s 464 (src:8441-8443)
GIVEN `the offence counselled is an indictable offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 464 the class of the offence of counselling an offence that is not committed` MEANS
    IF `the offence counselled is an indictable offence`
    THEN `an indictable offence`   -- (a)
    ELSE `an offence punishable on summary conviction`   -- (b)

§§ `s 465(1) -- Conspiracy`

-- src:8445 | 465 (1) Except where otherwise expressly provided by law, the following provisions apply in respect of conspiracy:
-- src:8446 | (a) every one who conspires with any one to commit murder or to cause another person to be murdered, whether in Canada or not, is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to a maximum term of imprisonment for life;
@ref s 465(1)(a) (src:8445-8446)
GIVEN `the person conspires with any one to commit murder or to cause another person to be murdered, whether in Canada or not` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the law expressly provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 465(1)(a) the person is guilty of the offence of conspiring to commit murder` MEANS
    IF `the law expressly provides otherwise`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Except where otherwise expressly provided by law"
    ELSE IF `the person conspires with any one to commit murder or to cause another person to be murdered, whether in Canada or not`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "conspires with any one to commit murder or to cause another person to be murdered, whether in Canada or not"

@ref s 465(1)(a) (src:8446)
GIVEN `the law expressly provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF Punishment)
`s 465(1)(a) the punishment for conspiring to commit murder` MEANS
    IF `the law expressly provides otherwise`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Except where otherwise expressly provided by law"
    ELSE JUST (LIST `s 463 punishment by indictment: imprisonment` `imprisonment for life`)

-- src:8447 | (b) every one who conspires with any one to prosecute a person for an alleged offence, knowing that they did not commit that offence, is guilty of
-- src:8448 | (i) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 10 years or an offence punishable on summary conviction, if the alleged offence is one for which, on conviction, that person would be liable to be sentenced to imprisonment for life or for a term of not more than 14 years, or
-- src:8449 | (ii) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than five years or an offence punishable on summary conviction, if the alleged offence is one for which, on conviction, that person would be liable to imprisonment for less than 14 years;
@ref s 465(1)(b) (src:8447-8449)
GIVEN `the person conspires with any one to prosecute a person for an alleged offence, knowing that they did not commit that offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the law expressly provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 465(1)(b) the person is guilty of the offence of conspiring to prosecute a person for an offence they did not commit` MEANS
    IF `the law expressly provides otherwise`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Except where otherwise expressly provided by law"
    ELSE IF `the person conspires with any one to prosecute a person for an alleged offence, knowing that they did not commit that offence`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "conspires with any one to prosecute a person for an alleged offence, knowing that they did not commit that offence"

@ref s 465(1)(b) (src:8448-8449)
GIVEN `the longest term of imprisonment to which the person alleged to have committed the offence would be liable on conviction` IS AN Imprisonment
      `the law expressly provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF Punishment)
`s 465(1)(b) the punishment for conspiring to prosecute a person for an offence they did not commit` MEANS
    IF `the law expressly provides otherwise`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Except where otherwise expressly provided by law"
    ELSE CONSIDER `the longest term of imprisonment to which the person alleged to have committed the offence would be liable on conviction`
         WHEN `no imprisonment is stated` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the alleged offence has no longest term stated in its section
         WHEN `imprisonment for life` THEN JUST (LIST `s 463 punishment by indictment: imprisonment` (`imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`), `s 463 punishment on summary conviction: none stated in the section`)   -- (i)
         WHEN `imprisonment for a term of` longest THEN
             IF `s 463 the term is less than fourteen years` longest
             THEN JUST (LIST `s 463 punishment by indictment: imprisonment` (`imprisonment for a term of` `five years`), `s 463 punishment on summary conviction: none stated in the section`)   -- (ii); see NOTES.md, finding on the overlap of (i) and (ii)
             ELSE IF `s 463 the term is fourteen years or less` longest
                  THEN JUST (LIST `s 463 punishment by indictment: imprisonment` (`imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`), `s 463 punishment on summary conviction: none stated in the section`)   -- (i)
                  ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a term above fourteen years that is not imprisonment for life is within neither (i) nor (ii)

-- src:8450 | (c) every one who conspires with any one to commit an indictable offence not provided for in paragraph (a) or (b) is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to the same punishment as that to which an accused who is guilty of that offence would, on conviction, be liable; and
@ref s 465(1)(c) (src:8450)
GIVEN `the person conspires with any one to commit an indictable offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence is provided for in paragraph (a) or (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the law expressly provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 465(1)(c) the person is guilty of the offence of conspiring to commit an indictable offence` MEANS
    IF `the law expressly provides otherwise`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Except where otherwise expressly provided by law"
    ELSE IF `the offence is provided for in paragraph (a) or (b)`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an indictable offence not provided for in paragraph (a) or (b)"
         ELSE IF `the person conspires with any one to commit an indictable offence`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "conspires with any one to commit an indictable offence"

@ref s 465(1)(c) (src:8450)
GIVEN `the class of the offence conspired to be committed` IS A `Class of offence`
      `the punishment of the offence conspired to be committed` IS A LIST OF Punishment
      `the law expressly provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF Punishment)
`s 465(1)(c) the punishment for conspiring to commit an indictable offence` MEANS
    IF `the law expressly provides otherwise`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Except where otherwise expressly provided by law"
    ELSE CONSIDER `the class of the offence conspired to be committed`
         WHEN `an indictable offence` THEN JUST `the punishment of the offence conspired to be committed`   -- "the same punishment as that to which an accused who is guilty of that offence would, on conviction, be liable"
         WHEN `an offence punishable on summary conviction` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (c) is about an indictable offence; a summary offence is paragraph (d)
         WHEN `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): paragraphs (c) and (d) name an indictable offence and an offence punishable on summary conviction; the text of s 463(d) treats a hybrid as a third class

-- src:8451 | (d) every one who conspires with any one to commit an offence punishable on summary conviction is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 465(1)(d) (src:8451)
GIVEN `the person conspires with any one to commit an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the law expressly provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 465(1)(d) the person is guilty of the offence of conspiring to commit an offence punishable on summary conviction` MEANS
    IF `the law expressly provides otherwise`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Except where otherwise expressly provided by law"
    ELSE IF `the person conspires with any one to commit an offence punishable on summary conviction`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "conspires with any one to commit an offence punishable on summary conviction"

@ref s 465(1)(d) (src:8451)
GIVEN `the law expressly provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF Punishment)
`s 465(1)(d) the punishment for conspiring to commit an offence punishable on summary conviction` MEANS
    IF `the law expressly provides otherwise`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Except where otherwise expressly provided by law"
    ELSE JUST (LIST `s 463 punishment on summary conviction: none stated in the section`)

-- src:8445 | 465 (1) Except where otherwise expressly provided by law, the following provisions apply in respect of conspiracy:
-- src:8446 | (a) every one who conspires with any one to commit murder or to cause another person to be murdered, whether in Canada or not, is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to a maximum term of imprisonment for life;
-- src:8447 | (b) every one who conspires with any one to prosecute a person for an alleged offence, knowing that they did not commit that offence, is guilty of
-- src:8448 | (i) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 10 years or an offence punishable on summary conviction, if the alleged offence is one for which, on conviction, that person would be liable to be sentenced to imprisonment for life or for a term of not more than 14 years, or
-- src:8449 | (ii) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than five years or an offence punishable on summary conviction, if the alleged offence is one for which, on conviction, that person would be liable to imprisonment for less than 14 years;
-- src:8450 | (c) every one who conspires with any one to commit an indictable offence not provided for in paragraph (a) or (b) is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to the same punishment as that to which an accused who is guilty of that offence would, on conviction, be liable; and
-- src:8451 | (d) every one who conspires with any one to commit an offence punishable on summary conviction is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 465(1) (src:8445-8451)
DECLARE `s 465(1) paragraph` IS ONE OF
    `s 465(1)(a) murder`
    `s 465(1)(b) conspiring to prosecute a person for an offence they did not commit`
    `s 465(1)(c) an indictable offence not provided for in (a) or (b)`
    `s 465(1)(d) an offence punishable on summary conviction`

-- (a) and (c) say "guilty of an indictable offence"; (b) says "an indictable offence ... or an offence punishable on summary conviction"; (d) says "an offence punishable on summary conviction".
@ref s 465(1) (src:8445-8451)
GIVEN paragraph IS A `s 465(1) paragraph`
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 465(1) the class of the offence of conspiracy` MEANS
    CONSIDER paragraph
    WHEN `s 465(1)(a) murder` THEN `an indictable offence`
    WHEN `s 465(1)(b) conspiring to prosecute a person for an offence they did not commit` THEN `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`
    WHEN `s 465(1)(c) an indictable offence not provided for in (a) or (b)` THEN `an indictable offence`
    WHEN `s 465(1)(d) an offence punishable on summary conviction` THEN `an offence punishable on summary conviction`

§§ `s 465(3) to (7) -- Conspiracy to commit offences, idem, jurisdiction, appearance, if previously tried outside Canada`

-- src:8452 | (2) [Repealed, 1985, c. 27 (1st Supp.), s. 61]
@ref s 465(2), shown repealed (src:8452)
`s 465(2) as the text shows it` MEANS "(2) [Repealed, 1985, c. 27 (1st Supp.), s. 61]"

-- src:8454 | (3) Every one who, while in Canada, conspires with any one to do anything referred to in subsection (1) in a place outside Canada that is an offence under the laws of that place shall be deemed to have conspired to do that thing in Canada.
@ref s 465(3) (src:8454)
GIVEN `while in Canada, the person conspires with any one` IS A BOOLEAN
      `to do anything referred to in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in a place outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that is an offence under the laws of that place` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 465(3) the person is deemed to have conspired in Canada` MEANS
    IF `while in Canada, the person conspires with any one` AND `to do anything referred to in subsection (1)` AND `in a place outside Canada` AND `that is an offence under the laws of that place`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every one who, while in Canada, conspires with any one to do anything referred to in subsection (1) in a place outside Canada that is an offence under the laws of that place shall be deemed to have conspired to do that thing in Canada"

-- src:8456 | (4) Every one who, while in a place outside Canada, conspires with any one to do anything referred to in subsection (1) in Canada shall be deemed to have conspired in Canada to do that thing.
@ref s 465(4) (src:8456)
GIVEN `while in a place outside Canada, the person conspires with any one` IS A BOOLEAN
      `to do anything referred to in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 465(4) the person is deemed to have conspired in Canada` MEANS
    IF `while in a place outside Canada, the person conspires with any one` AND `to do anything referred to in subsection (1)` AND `in Canada`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every one who, while in a place outside Canada, conspires with any one to do anything referred to in subsection (1) in Canada shall be deemed to have conspired in Canada to do that thing"

-- src:8458 | (5) Where a person is alleged to have conspired to do anything that is an offence by virtue of subsection (3) or (4), proceedings in respect of that offence may, whether or not that person is in Canada, be commenced in any territorial division in Canada, and the accused may be tried and punished in respect of that offence in the same manner as if the offence had been committed in that territorial division.
@ref s 465(5) (src:8458)
GIVEN `the person is alleged to have conspired to do anything that is an offence by virtue of subsection (3) or (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 465(5) proceedings may be commenced in any territorial division in Canada` MEANS
    IF `the person is alleged to have conspired to do anything that is an offence by virtue of subsection (3) or (4)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a person is alleged to have conspired to do anything that is an offence by virtue of subsection (3) or (4)"

-- src:8460 | (6) For greater certainty, the provisions of this Act relating to
-- src:8461 | (a) requirements that an accused appear at and be present during proceedings, and
-- src:8462 | (b) the exceptions to those requirements,
-- src:8463 | apply to proceedings commenced in any territorial division pursuant to subsection (5).
@ref s 465(6) (src:8460-8463)
GIVEN `the proceedings were commenced in a territorial division pursuant to subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 465(6) the provisions on the accused's appearance at and presence during proceedings, and their exceptions, apply` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings were commenced in a territorial division pursuant to subsection (5)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "apply to proceedings commenced in any territorial division pursuant to subsection (5)"

-- src:8465 | (7) If a person is alleged to have conspired to do anything that is an offence by virtue of subsection (3) or (4) and that person has been tried and dealt with outside Canada in respect of the offence in such a manner that, if the person had been tried and dealt with in Canada, they would be able to plead autrefois acquit, autrefois convict, pardon or an expungement order under the Expungement of Historically Unjust Convictions Act, the person shall be deemed to have been so tried and dealt with in Canada.
@ref s 465(7) (src:8465)
GIVEN `the person is alleged to have conspired to do anything that is an offence by virtue of subsection (3) or (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has been tried and dealt with outside Canada in respect of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in such a manner that, if tried and dealt with in Canada, they would be able to plead autrefois acquit, autrefois convict, pardon or an expungement order under the Expungement of Historically Unjust Convictions Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 465(7) the person is deemed to have been tried and dealt with in Canada` MEANS
    IF `the person is alleged to have conspired to do anything that is an offence by virtue of subsection (3) or (4)`
        AND `the person has been tried and dealt with outside Canada in respect of the offence`
        AND `in such a manner that, if tried and dealt with in Canada, they would be able to plead autrefois acquit, autrefois convict, pardon or an expungement order under the Expungement of Historically Unjust Convictions Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the person shall be deemed to have been so tried and dealt with in Canada"

§§ `ss 466 and 467 -- Conspiracy in restraint of trade; Saving`

-- src:8467 | 466 (1) A conspiracy in restraint of trade is an agreement between two or more persons to do or to procure to be done any unlawful act in restraint of trade.
@ref s 466(1) (src:8467)
GIVEN `the number of persons who are party to the agreement` IS A NUMBER
      `the agreement is to do or to procure to be done any unlawful act in restraint of trade` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 466(1) the agreement is a conspiracy in restraint of trade` MEANS
    IF `the number of persons who are party to the agreement` AT LEAST 2 AND `the agreement is to do or to procure to be done any unlawful act in restraint of trade`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A conspiracy in restraint of trade is an agreement between two or more persons to do or to procure to be done any unlawful act in restraint of trade"

-- src:8469 | (2) The purposes of a trade union are not, by reason only that they are in restraint of trade, unlawful within the meaning of subsection (1).
@ref s 466(2) (src:8469)
GIVEN `the purposes are the purposes of a trade union` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the only reason the purposes are unlawful is that they are in restraint of trade` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 466(2) the purposes of a trade union are unlawful within the meaning of subsection (1)` MEANS
    IF `the purposes are the purposes of a trade union` AND `the only reason the purposes are unlawful is that they are in restraint of trade`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The purposes of a trade union are not, by reason only that they are in restraint of trade, unlawful within the meaning of subsection (1)"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by reason only that they are in restraint of trade"

-- src:8471 | 467 (1) No person shall be convicted of the offence of conspiracy by reason only that he
-- src:8472 | (a) refuses to work with a workman or for an employer; or
-- src:8473 | (b) does any act or causes any act to be done for the purpose of a trade combination, unless that act is an offence expressly punishable by law.
@ref s 467(1) (src:8471-8473)
GIVEN `the conviction would be by reason only of the conduct in paragraph (a) or (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person refuses to work with a workman or for an employer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person does any act or causes any act to be done for the purpose of a trade combination` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that act is an offence expressly punishable by law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 467(1) the person is barred from being convicted of the offence of conspiracy` MEANS
    IF NOT `the conviction would be by reason only of the conduct in paragraph (a) or (b)`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by reason only that he"
    ELSE IF `the person refuses to work with a workman or for an employer`
         THEN JUST TRUE   -- (a); the "unless" is read as attaching to (b) only (see NOTES.md, fork register)
         ELSE IF `the person does any act or causes any act to be done for the purpose of a trade combination`
              THEN (IF `that act is an offence expressly punishable by law`
                    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless that act is an offence expressly punishable by law" (the unless is met, so the bar does not apply)
                    ELSE JUST TRUE)   -- (b)
              ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "refuses to work with a workman or for an employer"

-- src:8475 | (2) In this section, trade combination means any combination between masters or workmen or other persons for the purpose of regulating or altering the relations between masters or workmen, or the conduct of a master or workman in or in respect of his business, employment or contract of employment or service.
@ref s 467(2) (src:8475)
GIVEN `a combination between masters or workmen or other persons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `for the purpose of regulating or altering the relations between masters or workmen` IS A BOOLEAN
      `for the purpose of regulating or altering the conduct of a master or workman in or in respect of his business, employment or contract of employment or service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 467(2) the combination is a trade combination` MEANS
    IF `a combination between masters or workmen or other persons`
        AND (`for the purpose of regulating or altering the relations between masters or workmen`
             OR `for the purpose of regulating or altering the conduct of a master or workman in or in respect of his business, employment or contract of employment or service`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "trade combination means any combination between masters or workmen or other persons"
